//==
// # The neighbour table carried through refinement: types (complexity sweep, TKT-408)
//
// Idea 32 of docs/plans/step-mesher-ideas-evaluation.md. Each refinement pass built the
// neighbour table from scratch by a sort of 3T edge codes (NeighbourSlots): the surface pass,
// the angle pass and the surface refinement test, three times per pass on a curved face. The
// passes already keep the table current as they insert (WithNeighbours), so these types carry
// it from one pass to the next.
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - The carried table
//  - Refinement state

//==
// # The carried table

// A positioned triangulation and its neighbour table: Neighbours[3 t + j] is the triangle that
// holds side j of triangle t the other way round, or -1 (a boundary side).
// Invariant: Neighbours is NeighbourSlots(Positioned.Triangulation.Triangles,
// Positioned.Triangulation.Points.Count) slot for slot (Law_CarriedTableIsNeighbourSlots).
// Removes: the NeighbourSlots sort at the start of every pass and of every refinement test.
type PositionedTriangulationWithNeighbours
{
    Positioned: PositionedTriangulation;
    Neighbours: Array<Integer>;
}

//==
// # Refinement state

// The state of RefineToSurfaceByInsertionCarried after Rounds rounds: the triangulation the
// last round's angle pass left (Current), the one its surface pass left (Mid; Current before
// the first round), the marks the next round reads (triangles known to pass the surface test,
// refused by the angle pass, and known to meet the angle), and whether the last round added a
// point (true before the first round).
type CarriedRefinement
{
    Current: PositionedTriangulationWithNeighbours;
    Mid: PositionedTriangulationWithNeighbours;
    Known: Array<Boolean>;
    Refused: Array<Boolean>;
    Good: Array<Boolean>;
    Changed: Boolean;
    Rounds: Integer;
}
